    "lawSection": "Penal Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S7022B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the penal law, in relation to the crime of assault\non the operator of a for-hire vehicle\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo protect taxi drivers from being\nassaulted on the job by increasing criminal penalties for such\nassaults and posting warnings in taxi cabs about such penalties.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 titles the bill the \"taxi driver protection act.\"\n\nSection 2 amends subdivision 1 and paragraph (a) of subdivision 2 of\nsection 60.07 of the penal law, and adds a new subdivision 3, to (1)\nadd assault in the second and third degrees as specified offenses\nsubject to the related sentencing enhancement in this section, (2)\nlimiting the sentence for misdemeanor offenses under this chapter to\ntwice the maximum definite sentence otherwise authorized, and (3)\nrequire each for-hire vehicle to post a sign inside their vehicle\nwarning that \"assaulting a taxi driver is punishable by up to\ntwenty-five years in prison,\" although livery and black car drivers\nwill have the right, but not the obligation, to post such a sign.\n\nSection 3 amends section 10.00 of the penal law to add the phrase\n\"except as may otherwise be provided by law\" to the definition of\n\"misdemeanor.\n\nSection 4 provides for the act to take effect immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nAccording to the federal Occupational Safety and Health\nAdministration, taxi workers are thirty times more likely to be\nkilled on the job than other workers. New York City is home to the\nlargest taxi driver industry in the country.\n\nIncreasing penalties for attacks on taxi drivers underscores the\ngravity of the crime and, together with the requirement that a\nwarning be posted about the serious criminal penalties for assaulting\na taxi driver, will help to deter such crimes from occurring in the\nfuture.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Legislation.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
